WEBVTT

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.820
Good to have you back, Mr. Harper.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.700
Thank you, Bobby!

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.160
We haven't seen your mother here for quite some time.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.800
Well, maybe you just didn't recognize her.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.400
Like Satan, my mother can take many forms!

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.060
(chuckles)

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:17.740
Good one!

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:19.620
I'm ready to order.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:20.860
Of course!

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.620
Apologies for the frivolity!

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.000
What would you like?

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.720
I'll have the seared
ahi tuna fillet.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:27.640
Hmm... Good choice!

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.540
I want it very rare.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.280
That's how we serve it.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.040
I want it red in the
middle, not pink.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:31.580
Shall do.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.260
If it's pink, don't even
bother bringing it.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:33.980
Got it.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.900
Just give it to someone who
doesn't know what rare is.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:36.780
Of course.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.700
You know what? Forget it. You won't get it right.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.640
Is your salmon fresh?

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:42.960
Flown in today.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:43.720
What time?

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.260
I'll ask the chef.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.880
Many forms! Thought you were joking.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.240
Why can't I expose myself
to your kids?

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.440
I mean, why can't I meet
your kids?

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.380
Please don't make me
hurt your feelings.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.180
You can't hurt my feelings.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.880
All right, fine.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.760
You're a professional boy toy,

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.460
a perpetual adolescent leading a dissolute life.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.687
You may have your uses,

00:01:08.687 --> 00:01:11.580
but you're not the kind of man I want around my children.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.140
Oh.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.980
What made you think that would
hurt my feelings?

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.000
2 O'Clock. Jet Blue from Vancouver.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.720
Would you like me to find out
what the movie was?

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.840
Don't bother,
I'll just have the Capellini.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.640
And I'll have the pork chop
with a baked potato.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.240
(Bobby clears throat)

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.740
So, yay or nay
on the pork chop?

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.100
I'll have the spinach
and goat cheese salad.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.600
-Good choice.
-Thank you.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.600
On the food.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.080
Oh.
Hey, Mom.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.780
Uh, Mom, this is Lydia.
Lydia, my mother.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.620
Oh, pleased to meet you.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.060
Likewise!

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.580
Boy, I'm glad I stopped coming to work high.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.020
So, Lydia.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.180
What do you do?

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:02.900
I mean, besides my son.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:07.260
I'm in real estate.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.600
How interesting, so am I.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.180
Oh, yes. Evelyn Harper.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.600
I recognize you from your bus bench ads.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.600
People all over town are sitting on your face.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.440
Well, dear, maybe someday, if you work hard, people will be sitting on your face, too.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.860
Thank you. Although when I get to be your age,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.700
I hope I won't be schlepping
to open houses

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:34.620
in order to make a buck.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.840
(chuckles)
Don't say 'schlep', darling.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.200
You're a bit too vanilla to pull it off.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.820
So, Charlie, how long have you been seeing this lovely woman?

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.500
Uh... how long has it been, sweetie?

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.960
Are you telling me you don't remember when we met?

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.160
The way he drinks?

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.780
There's a good chance he doesn't remember coming down the stairs.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.180
Did his father drink?

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.740
What choice did he have?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.020
Charlie, don't be snide.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.020
And stand up straight.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.860
This is so weird.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.660
EVELYN:
Well, I really must run.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.360
Oh, me too. Can I walk you out?

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.640
Oh, how nice.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.200
Are you sure you don't want to stay and finish putting on your makeup?

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.520
That's okay, I'm done.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.840
Would you like to borrow some?

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:22.620
No, thanks, I'm allergic to the drugstore brands.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.020
What?

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:37.580
And they call you slow.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.100
You're kidding, right?

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:41.920
You don't see it?

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:42.900
See what?

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.140
Lydia and Mom.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:45.220
What about them?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.100
Come on, Charlie.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:50.640
The only difference between those two broads is you came out of one and...

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.900
CHARLIE:
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:52.740
Hold on, hold on.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.640
You think Lydia's like Mom?

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.980
No. We think Lydia is Mom.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.000
Okay, okay, you guys are nuts.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.760
This conversation
is over.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.940
Who calls me slow?